    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it's not about changing the input. the issue is the architecture itself. if the base code is fundamentally flawed, no matter what you input, you just get the same error. i keep looking at the logs of my life and it just looks like a memory leak. everything is just draining away for no reason. it feels like the only way to actually stop the error is to just kill the process. like, why keep the simulation running if it's just producing errors?",
